---
// PATH BEAM — the attribution story as motion, not as a claim.
//
// Two angled capsules. A pulse travels up each. The ORANGE path is split by a gap and its
// pulse vanishes at the break; the LIME path is unbroken and its pulse exits the top.
// Meaning: the browser-only path breaks, the first-party path holds.
//
// ⚠️ IT ASSERTS NOTHING. No destination is labelled, no platform named, no number shown, no
// delivery implied. That is deliberate — naming destinations is exactly what got hero-orbit
// cut (ad_platform_connections = 0, capi_deliveries = 0). A mechanism illustration can be
// true without a capability behind it; a labelled fan-out cannot.
//
// 🔴 CSS-ONLY. No island, no hydration, no timer, no JS of any kind. Because the motion is
// pure CSS @keyframes, a `prefers-reduced-motion` media query is SUFFICIENT — the two-layer
// problem from #697 (a media query cannot stop a setInterval that mutates state) does not
// arise here at all. If this ever needs JS, the design should change first.
//
// ── TOKENS, VERIFIED DECLARED (KI-112) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// The brief specified `--color-spend #FF7A33` for the orange. THAT TOKEN DOES NOT RESOLVE:
// --v3-spend aliases var(--color-spend), which is declared NOWHERE in marketing/src, and
// #FF7A33 appears in no v3 stylesheet. Using it would render `unset` — KI-112's mechanism
// for the fourth time. Uses --v3-orange-400 (#FF9459, concrete) instead, the nearest
// declared accent token, and --v3-accent (-> --color-primary -> #CCF03F) for the lime.
// (v1.5 repointed --color-primary from #D2EC2A; this comment tracks the live value.)
// Every custom property referenced here is verified concrete in BUILT output.
//
// GEOMETRY is the brief's, unchanged: 130-unit box; gap rect x=-10 y=53 w=150 h=13
// subtracted from the ORANGE capsule only; capsules x=26/66 y=18 w=22 h=84 rx=11,
// rotate(-28) about their own centres; pulses r=8 on the long axis; rails at 28%.
---
<div class="v3-beam" role="img" aria-label="Two signal paths: one breaks partway, the other completes.">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 130 130" width="100%" height="100%" aria-hidden="true">
    <defs>
      <!-- The break. Subtracted from the orange path ONLY, so its pulse disappears at the
           gap while the lime pulse travels the full length. -->
      <mask id="beam-break">
        <rect x="0" y="0" width="130" height="130" fill="#fff" />
        <rect x="-10" y="53" width="150" height="13" fill="#000" />
      </mask>
      <clipPath id="beam-rail-o"><rect x="26" y="18" width="22" height="84" rx="11" /></clipPath>
      <clipPath id="beam-rail-l"><rect x="66" y="18" width="22" height="84" rx="11" /></clipPath>
    </defs>

    <!-- ORANGE — the browser-only path. Broken. -->
    <g transform="rotate(-28 37 60)" mask="url(#beam-break)">
      <rect class="v3-beam-rail v3-beam-rail--o" x="26" y="18" width="22" height="84" rx="11" />
      <g clip-path="url(#beam-rail-o)">
        <circle class="v3-beam-pulse v3-beam-pulse--o" cx="37" cy="94" r="8" />
      </g>
    </g>

    <!-- LIME — the first-party path. Unbroken, and its pulse exits the top. -->
    <g transform="rotate(-28 77 60)">
      <rect class="v3-beam-rail v3-beam-rail--l" x="66" y="18" width="22" height="84" rx="11" />
      <g clip-path="url(#beam-rail-l)">
        <circle class="v3-beam-pulse v3-beam-pulse--l" cx="77" cy="94" r="8" />
      </g>
    </g>
  </svg>
</div>
